{
  "tema": 6865,
  "slug": "saber-conocer",
  "titulo": "Difference between saber and conocer (to know)",
  "subtitulo": "Sé que es tarde, conozco a Beto: facts vs people and places.",
  "foto": "t02.jpg",
  "regla": "Saber: facts, info (saber que, si, dónde…) and skills (saber + infinitive). Conocer: being familiar with people, places and things; with people it takes a.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "English has one verb, _to know_; Spanish has two."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Verb",
            "Use",
            "Example"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "saber",
              "facts and information",
              "Sé que es tarde."
            ],
            [
              "",
              "+ que / si / dónde / cuándo / cuál / quién / cómo",
              "¿Sabes si la taquería está abierta?"
            ],
            [
              "",
              "+ infinitive: skills (_to know how to_)",
              "Sé surfear."
            ],
            [
              "conocer",
              "people (with **a**)",
              "Conozco a Beto."
            ],
            [
              "",
              "places",
              "Conozco Ensenada."
            ],
            [
              "",
              "things you're familiar with by experience",
              "Conozco esa canción."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Conocer** can't introduce a fact with **que** or **si**, and **saber** can't be used for meeting or being familiar with a person."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Saber** + infinitive is about a learned skill: **sé nadar** (_I can swim_, I know how). **Poder** is about being able to right now."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Conocer** in the past often means _to meet_ someone for the first time: **conocí a Naomi en Ceres**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **saber** lives in your head; **conocer** lives in your experience."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
